{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WSM6WarmRain",
    "description": "Warm-rain process rates of the WRF single-moment 6-class microphysics scheme (WSM6; Hong and Lim 2006, Hong, Dudhia and Chen 2004), transcribed from the warm-rain block of mp_wsm6_run in phys/physics_mmm/mp_wsm6.F90 (WRF 4.8, NCAR/MMM-physics): autoconversion of cloud water to rain praut = qck1 qc^(7/3) above the threshold qc0 (HDC eq. 16), accretion of cloud water by rain pracw = pacrr lambda^-(3+b) qc (rho0/rho)^(1/2) (HL eq. A40), and evaporation/condensation of rain prevp = (rh - 1)(precr1 lambda^-2 + precr2 f_v coeres)/F (HDC eq. 14), all in kg/kg/s as pointwise functions of the layer state on the layer index `lev` (WRF k, layer 1 at the surface; no grid geometry is needed). The shared ingredients are factored into templates: the inverse slope lambda^-1 of the Marshall-Palmer raindrop distribution and its powers (microphysics_templates.esm), the transport properties of air (lib/wrf_air_properties.esm: kinematic viscosity, vapor diffusivity, thermal conductivity), the diffusional-growth denominator F and the ventilation factor; the scheme constants (n0r, a, b, r0, N_c, ...) come from wsm6_parameters.esm as subsystem `par` and the physical constants from lib/wrf_constants.esm as subsystem `wrf`. The derived rate coefficients qc0 = (4/3) pi rho_w r0^3 N_c / rho0, qck1 = 0.104 g E / (N_c rho_w)^(1/3) / mu rho0^(4/3), pacrr = pi n0r a Gamma(3+b) E_rc/4, precr1 = 2 pi n0r a_v and precr2 = 2 pi n0r b_v a^(1/2) Gamma(2.5+b/2) are observeds so that they can be checked against the values mp_wsm6_init computes. The saturation state (qsat, rh, xl) is an INPUT rather than computed here: WSM6 evaluates it once at the start of each sub-time step (saturation.esm) and does not refresh it after sedimentation, melting and freezing have changed the temperature, so the rates are evaluated at a temperature that differs from the one behind qsat/rh/xl (FORTRAN_BUGS.md note N4); a consumer binds saturation.esm's outputs at the state of its choice. The UNLIMITED rates praut, pracw, prevp are the physics; the kernel additionally applies per-process time-step limiters (a sink may not remove more than q/dtcld per sub-step, rain evaporation/condensation may not exceed half the vapor deficit/excess per sub-step), which are exposed separately as praut_lim, pracw_lim, prevp_lim with the sub-step length dtcld as a parameter -- they are time-step artefacts, not physics (FORTRAN_BUGS.md note N3), and the mass-conservation rescaling the kernel applies afterwards is not part of this component. Consumer-supplied inputs: the column fields T, qv, qc, qr, rho, p, qsat, rh, xl are REWRITE-TARGET ops `input_<name>` (esm-spec 4.2 open tier) that the consumer lowers -- in the inline tests through a per-test `expression_template_imports` library (tests/<id>_inputs.esm, generated by tools/fill_tests.py from the instrumented WRF dumps) because esm-spec 6.6 `parameter_overrides` admit scalars only.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["wrf", "microphysics", "wsm6", "warm-rain", "autoconversion", "accretion", "evaporation", "column"],
    "references": [
      { "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., and J.-O. J. Lim (2006). The WRF single-moment 6-class microphysics scheme (WSM6). J. Korean Meteor. Soc. 42, 129-151." },
      { "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., J. Dudhia, and S.-H. Chen (2004). A revised approach to ice microphysical processes for the bulk parameterization of clouds and precipitation. Mon. Wea. Rev. 132, 103-120.", "doi": "10.1175/1520-0493(2004)132<0103:ARATIM>2.0.CO;2" },
      { "citation": "NCAR/MMM-physics mp_wsm6.F90 at commit 550b5b4 (WRF 4.8 phys/physics_mmm submodule)." }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": { "type": "integer", "default": 40, "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte); 40 is the em_quarter_ss supercell reference column." }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "lev": { "kind": "interval", "size": "NLEV" }
  },
  "models": {
    "WSM6WarmRain": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        { "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_air_properties.esm" },
        { "ref": "./microphysics_templates.esm" }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": { "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm" },
        "par": { "ref": "./wsm6_parameters.esm" }
      },
      "variables": {
        "T": { "type": "unknown", "units": "K", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Absolute temperature at which the rates are evaluated (WSM6 t after the sub-step's sedimentation, melting and freezing)." },
        "qv": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Water-vapor mixing ratio (WSM6 q)." },
        "qc": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Cloud-water mixing ratio." },
        "qr": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Rain mixing ratio." },
        "rho": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/m^3", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Dry-air density (WSM6 den)." },
        "p": { "type": "unknown", "units": "Pa", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Pressure." },
        "qsat": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Saturation mixing ratio over water at the start-of-step state (saturation.esm qsat_w)." },
        "rh": { "type": "unknown", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Relative humidity with respect to water at the start-of-step state (saturation.esm rh_w)." },
        "xl": { "type": "unknown", "units": "J/kg", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Latent heat of vaporization at the start-of-step temperature (saturation.esm xl)." },
        "dtcld": { "type": "parameter", "units": "s", "default": 60.0, "description": "Length of the WSM6 sub-time step; enters only the rate limiters." },
        "pidn0r": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/m^7", "description": "pi rho_w n0r, the mass-weighted intercept of the raindrop distribution (WSM6 pidn0r)." },
        "rslope_max": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m", "description": "Inverse slope held where there is (almost) no rain, 1/lamdarmax (WSM6 rslopermax)." },
        "qc0": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg", "description": "Autoconversion threshold (4/3) pi rho_w r0^3 N_c / rho0 (WSM6 qc0)." },
        "qck1": { "type": "unknown", "units": "1/s", "description": "Autoconversion rate constant 0.104 g E_auto / (N_c rho_w)^(1/3) / mu rho0^(4/3) (WSM6 qck1)." },
        "pacrr": { "type": "unknown", "units": "1/(m^(19/5)*s)", "description": "Accretion coefficient pi n0r a Gamma(3 + b) E_rc / 4 (WSM6 pacrr); units for b = 4/5." },
        "precr1": { "type": "unknown", "units": "1/m^4", "description": "Rain evaporation coefficient of the non-ventilated term, 2 pi n0r a_v (WSM6 precr1)." },
        "precr2": { "type": "unknown", "units": "1/(m^(39/10)*s^(1/2))", "description": "Rain evaporation coefficient of the ventilated term, 2 pi n0r b_v a^(1/2) Gamma(2.5 + b/2) (WSM6 precr2); units for b = 4/5." },
        "denfac": { "type": "unknown", "units": "1", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Density correction of the fall speed, (rho0/rho)^(1/2) (WSM6 denfac)." },
        "rslope_r": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Inverse slope lambda^-1 of the raindrop distribution (WSM6 rslope(:,:,1))." },
        "rslopeb_r": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^(4/5)", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "lambda^-b (WSM6 rslopeb(:,:,1)); units for b = 4/5." },
        "rslope2_r": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^2", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "lambda^-2 (WSM6 rslope2(:,:,1))." },
        "rslope3_r": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^3", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "lambda^-3 (WSM6 rslope3(:,:,1))." },
        "nu": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^2/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Kinematic viscosity of air (WSM6 viscos(t, den))." },
        "Dv": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^2/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Diffusivity of water vapor in air (WSM6 diffus(t, p))." },
        "ka": { "type": "unknown", "units": "W/(m*K)", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Thermal conductivity of air (WSM6 xka(t, den))." },
        "f_diff": { "type": "unknown", "units": "s/m^2", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Diffusional-growth denominator rho xl^2/(ka r_v T^2) + 1/(qsat Dv) (WSM6 work1(:,:,1))." },
        "f_vent": { "type": "unknown", "units": "s^(1/2)/m", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Ventilation factor (nu/Dv)^(1/3) nu^(-1/2) (rho0/rho)^(1/4) (WSM6 work2)." },
        "coeres": { "type": "unknown", "units": "m^(29/10)", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Ventilation moment of the raindrop distribution lambda^-2 (lambda^-1 lambda^-b)^(1/2) (WSM6 coeres); units for b = 4/5." },
        "praut": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Autoconversion rate of cloud water to rain, unlimited (HDC eq. 16)." },
        "praut_lim": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Autoconversion rate after the kernel's time-step limiter min(praut, qc/dtcld) (WSM6 praut as applied)." },
        "pracw": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Accretion rate of cloud water by rain, unlimited (HL eq. A40)." },
        "pracw_lim": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Accretion rate after the kernel's time-step limiter min(pracw, qc/dtcld) (WSM6 pracw as applied)." },
        "prevp": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Rain evaporation (negative) / condensation (positive) rate, unlimited (HDC eq. 14)." },
        "satdt": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Vapor excess over saturation per sub-step, (max(qv, qmin) - qsat)/dtcld (WSM6 satdt)." },
        "prevp_lim": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg/kg/s", "shape": ["lev"], "description": "Rain evaporation/condensation rate after the kernel's time-step limiters (WSM6 prevp as applied)." }
      },
      "equations": [
        { "lhs": "T", "rhs": { "op": "input_T", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "qv", "rhs": { "op": "input_qv", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "qc", "rhs": { "op": "input_qc", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "qr", "rhs": { "op": "input_qr", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "rho", "rhs": { "op": "input_rho", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "p", "rhs": { "op": "input_p", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "qsat", "rhs": { "op": "input_qsat", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "rh", "rhs": { "op": "input_rh", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "xl", "rhs": { "op": "input_xl", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "pidn0r", "rhs": { "op": "*", "args": ["wrf.piconst", "wrf.rhowater", "par.n0r"] } },
        { "lhs": "rslope_max", "rhs": { "op": "/", "args": [1, "par.lamdarmax"] } },
        { "lhs": "qc0", "rhs": { "op": "/", "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": [4, 3] }, "wrf.piconst", "wrf.rhowater", { "op": "^", "args": ["par.r0", 3] }, "par.xncr"] },
          "wrf.rhoair0" ] } },
        { "lhs": "qck1", "rhs": { "op": "*", "args": [
          { "op": "/", "args": [
            { "op": "*", "args": ["par.autoconv_coef", "par.g_autoconv", "par.peaut"] },
            { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "^", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["par.xncr", "wrf.rhowater"] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, 3] }] }, "par.xmyu"] } ] },
          { "op": "^", "args": ["wrf.rhoair0", { "op": "/", "args": [4, 3] }] } ] } },
        { "lhs": "pacrr", "rhs": { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": ["wrf.piconst", "par.n0r", "par.avtr", "par.g3pbr", "par.eacrr"] }, 4] } },
        { "lhs": "precr1", "rhs": { "op": "*", "args": [2, "wrf.piconst", "par.n0r", "par.vent_a"] } },
        { "lhs": "precr2", "rhs": { "op": "*", "args": [2, "wrf.piconst", "par.n0r", "par.vent_b", { "op": "sqrt", "args": ["par.avtr"] }, "par.g5pbro2"] } },
        { "lhs": "denfac", "rhs": { "op": "sqrt", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["wrf.rhoair0", "rho"] }] } },
        { "lhs": "rslope_r", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "marshall_palmer_inverse_slope", "bindings": { "q": "qr", "rho": "rho", "pidn0": "pidn0r", "q_min": "par.qcrmin", "rslope_max": "rslope_max" } } },
        { "lhs": "rslopeb_r", "rhs": { "op": "^", "args": ["rslope_r", "par.bvtr"] } },
        { "lhs": "rslope2_r", "rhs": { "op": "^", "args": ["rslope_r", 2] } },
        { "lhs": "rslope3_r", "rhs": { "op": "^", "args": ["rslope_r", 3] } },
        { "lhs": "nu", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "kinematic_viscosity_of_air", "bindings": { "T": "T", "rho": "rho", "coef": "par.viscos_coef", "T_sutherland": "par.sutherland_T" } } },
        { "lhs": "Dv", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "diffusivity_of_water_vapor", "bindings": { "T": "T", "p": "p", "coef": "par.diffus_coef", "expn": "par.diffus_exp" } } },
        { "lhs": "ka", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "thermal_conductivity_of_air", "bindings": { "nu": "nu", "rho": "rho", "coef": "par.xka_coef" } } },
        { "lhs": "f_diff", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "diffusional_growth_denominator", "bindings": { "L": "xl", "T": "T", "rho": "rho", "ka": "ka", "r_v": "wrf.r_v", "qsat": "qsat", "Dv": "Dv" } } },
        { "lhs": "f_vent", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "ventilation_factor", "bindings": { "nu": "nu", "Dv": "Dv", "rho": "rho", "rho0": "wrf.rhoair0" } } },
        { "lhs": "coeres", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "ventilation_slope_factor", "bindings": { "rslope": "rslope_r", "rslopeb": "rslopeb_r", "rslope2": "rslope2_r" } } },
        { "lhs": "praut", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "hdc_autoconversion", "bindings": { "qc": "qc", "qc0": "qc0", "qck1": "qck1" } } },
        { "lhs": "praut_lim", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sink_rate_limiter", "bindings": { "rate": "praut", "q": "qc", "dt": "dtcld" } } },
        { "lhs": "pracw", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "accretion_of_cloud_by_rain", "bindings": { "qc": "qc", "qr": "qr", "rslope3": "rslope3_r", "rslopeb": "rslopeb_r", "pacrr": "pacrr", "denfac": "denfac", "qr_min": "par.qcrmin", "qc_min": "par.qmin" } } },
        { "lhs": "pracw_lim", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "sink_rate_limiter", "bindings": { "rate": "pracw", "q": "qc", "dt": "dtcld" } } },
        { "lhs": "prevp", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "rain_evaporation", "bindings": { "qr": "qr", "rh": "rh", "rslope2": "rslope2_r", "coeres": "coeres", "f_vent": "f_vent", "f_diff": "f_diff", "precr1": "precr1", "precr2": "precr2" } } },
        { "lhs": "satdt", "rhs": { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": [{ "op": "max", "args": ["qv", "par.qmin"] }, "qsat"] }, "dtcld"] } },
        { "lhs": "prevp_lim", "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "rain_evaporation_limiter", "bindings": { "prevp": "prevp", "qr": "qr", "satdt": "satdt", "dt": "dtcld" } } }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "qss_step250_row23_col24_mature_warm_rain",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_quarter_ss idealized supercell (GNU real32 build, dx = 2 km, dt = 12 s, 40 layers, WSM6 only, no radiation/surface physics) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump with esm_dump_inner hooks inside mp_wsm6_run of the ctessum-claude/MMM-physics fork, commit 52cfbd7) and replayed through the real64 (kind_phys = real64) standalone kernels/wsm6_driver at the WRF step. The test is POINTWISE and step-free: the inputs are the evaluation state the kernel dumps immediately before its warm-rain block (t_rates, q_rates, qc_rates, qr_rates: the state after the sub-step's sedimentation, melting and freezing; den and p: kernel arguments; qsat_w, rh_w, xl: the start-of-sub-step saturation block, see saturation.esm), the expected values are the process rates the kernel dumps right after evaluating them (`<rate>_raw`: after each process's own time-step limiter, before the mass-conservation rescaling) and the intermediates rslope*, work1 (f_diff), work2 (f_vent), denfac and the mp_wsm6_init coefficients, all taken from the real64 replay. No small-dt replay is used because WSM6's increments are not rate x dt (FORTRAN_BUGS.md note N3). Real64 replay vs real32 in-model dump (compare_dump.py): 1.5e-7 (praut), 8e-7 (pracw), 7.5e-6 (prevp), 3-4e-7 (rslope*), 1.5e-6 (work1), 3.6e-7 (work2); the real32 driver reproduces the dump bit-for-bit. Residual mismatch between this component and the real64 kernel comes from the kernel's default-real literals and the real32 WRF constants it receives (bvtr = 0.800000011920929, avtr = 841.9000244, den0 = 1.27999997, cpv = 1846.4000244, rv = 461.6000061, .104, 9.8, .55, .78, .31, 1.496e-6, 8.794e-5, 1.414e3), which this component takes at their nominal values from lib/wrf_constants.esm and wsm6_parameters.esm (FORTRAN_BUGS.md note N2-style rounding); measured with zero tolerances over all four tests it is <= 4.1e-7 relative in the rates (praut; pracw 1.2e-7, prevp 2.1e-7), 1.9e-7 in the coefficients (qck1), 2e-7 of the column maximum in f_diff, 1e-7 in f_vent and <= 9e-8 in rslope*, denfac. Tolerances are set 5-10x above the measured residual: relative 1e-6 on the mp_wsm6_init coefficients and on every spot check, absolute Linf_error bounds on the whole columns at 1e-6 of each column's maximum. The unlimited rates praut, pracw, prevp are the physics and are spot-checked at layers where the kernel's limiter is provably inactive (there the dumped `<rate>_raw` equals the unlimited rate); the limited observeds praut_lim, pracw_lim, prevp_lim are compared with the dumped `<rate>_raw` over the whole column. Regime: supercell step 250 (t = 50 min), tile row j = 23, tile column i = 24 (the column with the strongest warm-rain rates): qc up to 2.4e-3, qr up to 1.3e-2 kg/kg, autoconversion active in layers 3-18 (qc > qc0), accretion and rain evaporation/condensation in layers 1-16 (rain present), rh_w 0.68-1.36 so prevp changes sign within the column, freezing level at layer 9. No limiter is active anywhere in the column (checked in the dump: no praut/pracw equals qc/dtcld and no prevp equals -qr/dtcld or satdt/2), so the whole `<rate>_raw` columns equal the unlimited rates.",
          "parameter_overrides": {
            "dtcld": 12.0
          },
          "expression_template_imports": [
            {
              "ref": "./tests/qss_step250_row23_col24_mature_warm_rain_inputs.esm"
            }
          ],
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 1.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "pidn0r",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 25132741928.100586,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rslope_max",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.25e-05,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "qc0",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0005026548609702604,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "qck1",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 6.773894126490344,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "pacrr",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 24813389640.68711,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "precr1",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 39207075.969729885,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "precr2",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 825851896.7563319,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "denfac",
              "time": 0.0,
              "reduce": "Linf_error",
              "expected": 0.0,
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "k"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "k": {
                    "from": "lev"
                  }
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "const",
                      "args": [],
                      "value": [1.074297648601964, 1.0988758165188706, 1.1288867811848777, 1.1602700614599697, 1.192123954468512, 1.2246820558855798, 1.2582500928449838, 1.292808506687401, 1.3283037231725008, 1.3645763776496205, 1.4020583602973977, 1.4396854385640094, 1.4835556358342181, 1.5248115440101326, 1.5664510609796232, 1.6091176379658874, 1.6525457933489218, 1.6967181474622186, 1.74166539824332, 1.787388938078431, 1.833815931787568, 1.8819464686130778, 1.930171827665902, 1.9789910276164668, 2.0287444851154315, 2.08004478930757, 2.1338844217674344, 2.192584031512916, 2.272919650733487, 2.4071314861423874, 2.517537815782692, 2.628772485136029, 2.7445896462038344, 2.862603538137479, 2.982749200059628, 3.1061754351938746, 3.2347614364631796, 3.3704631345827436, 3.515037802394403, 3.669399516419166]
                    },
                    "k"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 4e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rslope_r",
              "time": 0.0,
              "reduce": "Linf_error",
              "expected": 0.0,
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "k"
