        {
          "id": "scm_call120_no_condensate_zero_rates",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_quarter_ss idealized supercell (GNU real32 build, dx = 2 km, dt = 12 s, 40 layers, WSM6 only, no radiation/surface physics) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump with esm_dump_inner hooks inside mp_wsm6_run of the ctessum-claude/MMM-physics fork, commit 52cfbd7) and replayed through the real64 (kind_phys = real64) standalone kernels/wsm6_driver at the WRF step. The test is POINTWISE and step-free: the inputs are the evaluation state the kernel dumps immediately before its warm-rain block (t_rates, q_rates, qc_rates, qr_rates: the state after the sub-step's sedimentation, melting and freezing; den and p: kernel arguments; qsat_w, rh_w, xl: the start-of-sub-step saturation block, see saturation.esm), the expected values are the process rates the kernel dumps right after evaluating them (`<rate>_raw`: after each process's own time-step limiter, before the mass-conservation rescaling) and the intermediates rslope*, work1 (f_diff), work2 (f_vent), denfac and the mp_wsm6_init coefficients, all taken from the real64 replay. No small-dt replay is used because WSM6's increments are not rate x dt (FORTRAN_BUGS.md note N3). Real64 replay vs real32 in-model dump (compare_dump.py): 1.5e-7 (praut), 8e-7 (pracw), 7.5e-6 (prevp), 3-4e-7 (rslope*), 1.5e-6 (work1), 3.6e-7 (work2); the real32 driver reproduces the dump bit-for-bit. Residual mismatch between this component and the real64 kernel comes from the kernel's default-real literals and the real32 WRF constants it receives (bvtr = 0.800000011920929, avtr = 841.9000244, den0 = 1.27999997, cpv = 1846.4000244, rv = 461.6000061, .104, 9.8, .55, .78, .31, 1.496e-6, 8.794e-5, 1.414e3), which this component takes at their nominal values from lib/wrf_constants.esm and wsm6_parameters.esm (FORTRAN_BUGS.md note N2-style rounding); measured with zero tolerances over all four tests it is <= 4.1e-7 relative in the rates (praut; pracw 1.2e-7, prevp 2.1e-7), 1.9e-7 in the coefficients (qck1), 2e-7 of the column maximum in f_diff, 1e-7 in f_vent and <= 9e-8 in rslope*, denfac. Tolerances are set 5-10x above the measured residual: relative 1e-6 on the mp_wsm6_init coefficients and on every spot check, absolute Linf_error bounds on the whole columns at 1e-6 of each column's maximum. The unlimited rates praut, pracw, prevp are the physics and are spot-checked at layers where the kernel's limiter is provably inactive (there the dumped `<rate>_raw` equals the unlimited rate); the limited observeds praut_lim, pracw_lim, prevp_lim are compared with the dumped `<rate>_raw` over the whole column. Regime: the em_scm_xy single-column run (mp = 6, dt = 60 s, 59 layers) at call 120 (step 60, 20:00 UTC) has no liquid condensate anywhere (qc = qr = 0, qi <= 5e-5), so every warm-rain rate must be exactly zero, the inverse slope equals rslope_max in every layer, and only the state-dependent intermediates (denfac, f_diff, f_vent) carry information. The component's lev axis has 40 layers (the supercell size, esm-spec 6.6 tests cannot rebind a metaparameter), so this test uses the lowest 40 of the 59 SCM layers; the rates are pointwise, so the truncation is exact.",
